<title>Perl script for using MaBoSS</title>
</head>
<a href="PlMaBoSS_1.1.pl">PlMaBoSS_1.1.pl</a><br>
MaBoSS should be installed and available through a command line.<br>
Running perl script: "./PlMaBoSS.pl file_bnd.bnd file_cfg.cfg threshold=0.1"<br>
This will create a directory, with the same name as the cfg file (adding a number if directory already exists).<br>
The directory contains input files and output files. It also contains csv-processed files (file_cfg_probtraj_table.csv and file_cfg_statdist_table.cfg) and the list of fixed points (file_cfg.FP). The threshold is used in the file "file_cfg_statdist_table.cfg", in order to suppress states whose probability is below the threshold.<br>
